1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,180
Hi everyone, I'm Ria!

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:09,990
I changed my phone today

3
00:00:09,990 --> 00:00:14,730
I switched to a new phone

4
00:00:14,730 --> 00:00:16,450
Ta-da!

5
00:00:16,450 --> 00:00:20,630
I'm so happy right now

6
00:00:20,630 --> 00:00:22,660
Ta-da!

7
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:31,780
Do you guys like Samsung? Or do you prefer Apple?

8
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:42,120
Today's podcast topic is the brand image of Samsung and Apple

9
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,560
Image

10
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,880
First, Samsung

11
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:54,130
What kind of image does Samsung have in Korea?

12
00:00:54,130 --> 00:01:01,680
Do all Koreans like Samsung phones?

13
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:13,920
To be honest, Samsung has a strong image of being used by older people

14
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:19,760
And people say this a lot too

15
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:24,220
Samsung is a bit dated

16
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:26,190
Dated

17
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:34,460
Here, 'chon-seu-reop-da' refers to something that feels a bit old-fashioned

18
00:01:34,460 --> 00:01:51,580
For example, when clothes or designs look like they're out of style, we say it's a bit dated

19
00:01:51,580 --> 00:02:00,870
So in Korea, young people prefer the iPhone much more

20
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:05,930
I met some friends not too long ago

21
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:09,690
I met them for the first time in a while

22
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:19,690
When we were younger, all my friends used Samsung phones, the Galaxy

23
00:02:19,690 --> 00:02:31,330
But when I met them recently, I was the only one using a Galaxy phone

24
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:32,960
Seriously

25
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:39,080
All those friends had switched to iPhones

26
00:02:39,080 --> 00:02:47,480
Because in Korea, iPhones usually have this kind of image

27
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:50,240
Sophisticated vibe

28
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:58,740
'Se-ryeon-dwaet-da' means having good style and looking cool

29
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:07,560
It's the opposite of the word 'dated' that we just learned

30
00:03:07,560 --> 00:03:16,700
So the iPhone has a sophisticated and very trendy image

31
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,370
In the past

32
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:20,520
Samsung phones

33
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,670
Front and back

34
00:03:22,670 --> 00:03:30,590
If you looked at the back, the logo was in the middle just like Apple

35
00:03:30,590 --> 00:03:34,130
Middle

36
00:03:34,130 --> 00:03:48,420
And Apple still proudly puts their logo right in the center

37
00:03:48,420 --> 00:03:51,370
The apple-shaped logo

38
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:57,440
That famous apple-shaped logo is there

39
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:10,720
But as time went by, Samsung started hiding the logo so it's less visible

40
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,340
Hid it

41
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:14,670
Logo placement

42
00:04:14,670 --> 00:04:15,940
Placement

43
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:18,750
Where did they move it?

44
00:04:18,750 --> 00:04:20,030
Down

45
00:04:20,030 --> 00:04:25,220
They also moved the logo placement further down

46
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:27,120
Lowered it

47
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:28,360
Color

48
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:32,860
They even changed the logo color to be faint

49
00:04:32,860 --> 00:04:34,550
Faintly

50
00:04:34,550 --> 00:04:39,170
Now you can't really see the logo well

51
00:04:39,170 --> 00:04:45,210
I actually like this logo

52
00:04:45,210 --> 00:04:50,140
But it's a bit of a shame that they keep hiding it

53
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,770
It's a shame

54
00:04:51,770 --> 00:04:56,770
So I had this thought

55
00:04:56,770 --> 00:05:05,590
"Ah, Samsung wants to escape that 'dated' image."

56
00:05:05,590 --> 00:05:07,020
Escape

57
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:12,100
They are trying to escape the dated image

58
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:13,440
Escape

59
00:05:13,440 --> 00:05:23,360
Now, let's check together if what I said is true

60
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:25,310
Check it out

61
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:30,750
I'll do a search

62
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:40,140
I'm searching for "People who use Galaxy" right now

63
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:47,140
If you search like this, a lot of interesting posts come up

64
00:05:47,140 --> 00:05:48,790
Two weeks ago

65
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:52,450
This post was uploaded two weeks ago

66
00:05:52,450 --> 00:06:06,680
This is an actual post written by a Korean on the internet

67
00:06:06,680 --> 00:06:13,900
"Even these days, do college students or people in their 20s think Galaxy users are a bit lame?"

68
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:17,250
That's the title of the post

69
00:06:17,250 --> 00:06:19,360
Title

70
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:22,020
Shall we look at it one by one?

71
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,560
Yo-sae

72
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:28,490
'Yo-sae' means 'these days'

73
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:35,570
It says "a tendency to look at them as 'lame'"

74
00:06:35,570 --> 00:06:37,790
Lame

75
00:06:37,790 --> 00:06:45,840
This word sounds a bit strong

76
00:06:45,840 --> 00:06:51,310
You guys know the expression 'byeol-lo-da', right?

77
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:57,760
Usually, we say, "Ah... that's not that great."

78
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:03,420
'Gu-ri-da' is even worse than 'byeol-lo-da'

79
00:07:03,420 --> 00:07:09,510
It feels dated and not cool at all

80
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:16,180
It's a word used when you want to express that feeling strongly

81
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,690
Look at my expression

82
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:20,810
Ugh, so lame

83
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:23,400
The design is so lame

84
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,800
It's tacky

85
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:28,810
It has that kind of strong nuance

86
00:07:28,810 --> 00:07:40,730
Anyway, to be honest, I've never used an iPhone once in my entire life

87
00:07:40,730 --> 00:07:45,090
This is my older sister's phone

88
00:07:45,090 --> 00:07:46,900
My sister's phone

89
00:07:46,900 --> 00:07:49,700
Why is that?

90
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:50,820
Reason

91
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:54,260
There are a few reasons

92
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:57,710
First, I'm used to it

93
00:07:57,710 --> 00:08:04,000
I've always used Samsung phones, so I'm used to them

94
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,260
I've grown accustomed to it

95
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:11,180
Second, it's convenient

96
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:17,150
Samsung Pay is really convenient in Korea

97
00:08:17,150 --> 00:08:25,450
You can pay anytime, anywhere

98
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:36,730
Because of that, it's been a very long time since I used a wallet

99
00:08:36,730 --> 00:08:42,500
As long as I have my phone, I can pay for everything

100
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:47,040
I can also take the bus and subway

101
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:50,450
And another convenient point

102
00:08:50,450 --> 00:09:00,800
Earphones, smartwatches, tablets—all these things sync together

103
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,700
Sync

104
00:09:02,700 --> 00:09:11,810
Syncing means that various devices work together

105
00:09:11,810 --> 00:09:14,070
They work together

106
00:09:14,070 --> 00:09:19,390
So it's really convenient to use

107
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:20,540
Convenient

108
00:09:20,540 --> 00:09:21,980
If

109
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:29,440
What if I switch to Apple? Then there are many problems

110
00:09:29,440 --> 00:09:33,930
I'd have to switch everything at once

111
00:09:33,930 --> 00:09:40,130
Phone, earphones, watch, tablet... it's very expensive, right?

112
00:09:40,130 --> 00:09:44,010
So it's a bit of a burden

113
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:45,830
Burden

114
00:09:45,830 --> 00:09:48,470
The price is a burden

115
00:09:48,470 --> 00:09:50,590
The cost is a burden

116
00:09:50,590 --> 00:09:57,340
Third, I like the Galaxy design

117
00:09:57,340 --> 00:10:04,250
I especially like this kind of angular design

118
00:10:04,250 --> 00:10:06,540
Angular design

119
00:10:06,540 --> 00:10:11,800
Oh but, this phone's design is rounded

120
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:14,010
This is angle

121
00:10:14,010 --> 00:10:15,780
Angular

122
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:17,150
Round

123
00:10:17,150 --> 00:10:25,150
Anyway, and on this Samsung phone... the Pen!

124
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:27,010
There is a Pen

125
00:10:27,010 --> 00:10:30,080
I really love that

126
00:10:30,080 --> 00:10:37,920
I can write directly on the phone

127
00:10:37,920 --> 00:10:40,370
I can write

128
00:10:40,370 --> 00:10:49,090
So until now, I've only used phones that have a Pen

129
00:10:49,090 --> 00:10:52,640
Now it's quiz time

130
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:59,940
I'm going to write something in the phone notes now

131
00:11:02,050 --> 00:11:08,390
Why is my handwriting so weird?

132
00:11:08,390 --> 00:11:13,390
I am Korean, I promise

133
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:15,100
Ta-da

134
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:19,530
What did I write here?

135
00:11:19,530 --> 00:11:28,350
If you can read this right now, please leave a comment

136
00:11:28,350 --> 00:11:30,100
I love you too

137
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:33,410
Leave a comment like that

138
00:11:33,410 --> 00:11:45,690
Then I will accept your heart and compliment your Korean skills!

139
00:11:45,690 --> 00:11:46,640
Compliment

140
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:52,350
But there is a funny saying in Korea

141
00:11:52,350 --> 00:11:53,740
Slang?

142
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:56,080
There's a slang term

143
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,950
Apple Fever

144
00:11:57,950 --> 00:12:05,730
'Apple-byeong' refers to the state of wanting to buy Apple products so badly

145
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:10,690
So Korean people say it like this

146
00:12:10,690 --> 00:12:15,010
"I've caught Apple fever lately."

147
00:12:15,010 --> 00:12:19,360
If you look online, there are posts like this

148
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:23,680
My Apple fever has been fully cured

149
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:33,400
Here, 'wan-chi' means being completely cured of a disease

150
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:39,740
So the meaning of this sentence is this

151
00:12:39,740 --> 00:12:41,570
Finally!

152
00:12:41,570 --> 00:12:45,000
I finally bought an Apple product

153
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:49,800
So in Korea, there's also a saying like this

154
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:54,120
"Apple fever is only cured by buying."

155
00:12:54,120 --> 00:13:00,240
In other words, you have to buy an Apple product to cure this 'illness'

156
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:02,200
It's a joke like that

157
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:09,500
Actually, I caught Apple fever once too

158
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:12,680
About two years ago?

159
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:22,980
But rather than Apple fever, I actually really needed it

160
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,730
I needed it

161
00:13:24,730 --> 00:13:31,370
At that time, I was teaching classes with young students

162
00:13:31,370 --> 00:13:32,610
Class

163
00:13:32,610 --> 00:13:41,060
I had a class where we sang and recorded English pop songs together

164
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:44,610
But there was a problem

165
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:46,400
Problem

166
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:57,850
There was an app for recording and producing songs, but that app was only available on Apple

167
00:13:57,850 --> 00:14:02,710
Have you guys ever felt this way?

168
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:12,940
Isn't it so frustrating when the apps on Apple and Galaxy are different?

169
00:14:12,940 --> 00:14:15,170
It's so frustrating

170
00:14:15,170 --> 00:14:16,720
It's annoying

171
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:23,150
So I eventually bought an Apple tablet

172
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:32,260
I bought the cheapest model at the time

173
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:36,310
It was the basic iPad model

174
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:41,410
And that's how my Apple fever was cured

175
00:14:41,410 --> 00:14:43,600
Cured

176
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:49,120
Now, please let me hear your thoughts

177
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:55,270
Samsung vs. Apple, what's your choice?

178
00:14:55,270 --> 00:15:03,200
Is there another smartphone brand you like besides these two?

179
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:09,140
And I'm especially curious about this too

180
00:15:09,140 --> 00:15:18,560
What is the image of Samsung Galaxy phones in your country?

181
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:25,510
Does it feel like something older people use, like in Korea?

182
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:27,930
Or is it different?

183
00:15:27,930 --> 00:15:33,890
You can be really, really honest

184
00:15:33,890 --> 00:15:37,510
I won't get hurt

185
00:15:37,510 --> 00:15:39,220
I won't get hurt

186
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:40,630
Probably?

187
00:15:40,630 --> 00:15:44,860
But I'm already crying

188
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:48,530
Please let me know in the comments

189
00:15:48,530 --> 00:15:52,080
Thank you so much for today too

190
00:15:52,080 --> 00:15:57,120
I'm always rooting for your Korean!

191
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:07,180
Bye! :)
